NAME
       pthtest - exercise POSIX threads

SYNOPSIS
       pthtest [threads] [iterations]

DESCRIPTION
       Starts the given number of threads (4 by default) and checks three
       things in turn: that a mutex keeps a shared counter exact under
       contention, that concurrent malloc and free do not corrupt the heap,
       and that a condition variable broadcast wakes every waiter.

       Each thread performs iterations increments of the counter; the
       default is 20000.

SEE ALSO
       sigtest(1), semtest(1)
